.page sha256sum 1 compute and check SHA-256 message digests

# SYNOPSIS
*sha256sum* [*-b*] [_FILE_...]
*sha256sum* *-c* [_LISTFILE_]

# DESCRIPTION
`sha256sum` prints the SHA-256 digest of each _FILE_ as 64 hexadecimal digits, two spaces and the file name. With no file it reads standard input and prints `-` as the name. It works exactly like md5sum(1) with a stronger algorithm.

# OPTIONS
@ *-c*
    Check the files listed in _LISTFILE_ (or standard input); each is reported as `NAME: OK` or `NAME: FAILED`.
@ *-b*
    Accepted for compatibility.

# EXIT STATUS
0 if all went well, 1 if a file was unreadable or a check failed.

# EXAMPLES
    echo -n abc | sha256sum
    sha256sum /bin/* > /tmp/sums
    sha256sum -c /tmp/sums | grep -v OK

# SEE ALSO
md5sum(1), crc32(1), cmp(1)
